WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.980
At each division of the bristle lineage, one sister hears Notch.

2
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.640
But where in the lineage does Notch act?

3
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.460
Notch is a receptor that signals only between touching cells.

4
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.020
A ligand called Delta, on the neighbour, activates it.

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.860
When it is activated, it is cut.

6
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.700
Its inner part can then switch genes on.

7
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:30.610
In 1990, Volker Hartenstein and James Posakony used a temperature-sensitive allele

8
00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:31.610
of Notch.

9
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.080
The mutant protein works at a low temperature and fails at a higher one.

10
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.290
So warming the animal removes Notch for a chosen window.

11
00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.210
They warmed fly pupae in short pulses.

12
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.240
First, pulses in the first 14 hours after the pupa formed.

13
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.280
That is before the bristle precursors divide.

14
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:55.433
These gave extra precursors in place of skin cells.

15
00:00:56.367 --> 00:01:00.767
Normally the new precursor signals to its neighbours through Notch, and they stay

16
00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:04.447
skin cells. Without Notch, they become precursors too.

17
00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:08.370
Each extra precursor formed a normal bristle.

18
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:12.190
Now warm the pupae from 14 to 20 hours.

19
00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:15.430
That is around the time the precursors divide.

20
00:01:16.483 --> 00:01:19.023
Notch now fails at the divisions of the lineage.

21
00:01:20.043 --> 00:01:21.803
What cells should the sense organs contain?

22
00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:30.247
The sense organs were made only of neurons.

23
00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.627
There was no shaft and no socket.

24
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:36.927
Walk it down the map.

25
00:01:36.927 --> 00:01:41.187
With no Notch, the first division gives two inner precursors.

26
00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:46.327
Each inner precursor then gives two neurons, not a neuron and a sheath cell.

27
00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.187
So the neuron is a Notch-off fate.

28
00:01:50.007 --> 00:01:53.147
The outer branch, which makes the shaft and socket, needs Notch.

29
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.540
Notch is used once to pick the precursor.

30
00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.460
It is used again to split its progeny.

31
00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:07.090
In 1996, Ming Guo, Lily Jan and Yuh Nung Jan went further.

32
00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.030
Notch works as a two-way switch at each division.

33
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.380
That fills in the map.

34
00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.520
At the first division, the inner precursor is the Notch-off daughter.

35
00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.980
The outer precursor hears Notch.

36
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.480
At the outer precursor's division, the hair cell is Notch-off.

37
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.640
The socket cell hears Notch.

38
00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.950
At the inner precursor's division, the neuron is Notch-off.

39
00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:31.970
The sheath cell hears Notch.

40
00:02:32.983 --> 00:02:35.703
So at every division, one daughter hears Notch.

41
00:02:36.563 --> 00:02:39.363
The sisters sit side by side, and either could signal.

42
00:02:40.163 --> 00:02:41.283
What stops one from hearing?

43
00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:44.683
Notch is a switch used at every division.

44
00:02:45.643 --> 00:02:47.483
One daughter hears it, and one does not.
